<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97331" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρῶμα</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ατος</span>, τό, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρώννυμι</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>anything spread</i> or
				<i>laid out for lying</i> or <i>sitting upon, mattress,
			bed</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀσπάλαθοι δὲ τάπησιν ὁμοῖον στρῶμα
					θανόντι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					1193
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>PEleph.</u>
				5.5
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, etc.; used on the funeral bier, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(5).593.3
			</span></i> (Ceos, <span class="entity">v B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Schwyzer</u>
				323
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>C</u>
				29
			</span></i> (Delph., <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>): pl., <i>bedclothes,
				coverings of a dinner-couch</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ach.</u>
				1090
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1069
			</span></i>, al.; of a bird's nest, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>HA</u>
				616a2
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. πορφυρόβαπτα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
				</span></i>
			 Com.<i><span class="en">
				208
			</span></i>; coupled with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱμάτια,
			ἔπιπλα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Lys.
				32.16
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἴρεσθαι τὰ ς</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ra.</u>
				596
			</span></i> (lyr.); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. ὑποσπᾶν</span> to pull
			the <i>bed</i> from under one, <i><span class="en">
				D.
				24.197
			</span></i>: cf. 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στρωματεύς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					1
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>horsecloth, horse-trappings</i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.8.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antiph.
				109
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				1.183
			</span></i>; <i>trappings</i> of an ass, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				38
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>pavement,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				12.313.71
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				22.1666<i>B</i>37
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				7.4255.6
			</span></i> (Oropus, <span class="entity">iv B.C.</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>Inscr.Délos</u>
				502
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>A</u>
				24
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				12(8).380
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Thasos</span>), etc.</div>
